//! check: run(exit=0, stdout="normal=0 breach=2\n")
//! phase: run
//! conforms: conc.proc.exit, mem.region.cap.3, mod.dir
//!
//! #219 (lobo ws13, s134): a proc spawned from a NON-ENTRY module —
//! #136's proc twin. `work.run` lives in the `work/` module and
//! spawns `body` as a proc; the entry only calls it. Before s134 the
//! release tier refused `func.addr of @work.run.task0.entry outside
//! this object's subset` whenever the partition separated the spawner
//! from its entry shim (the shim is synthetic, `src_file = None`, and
//! rides the root module's unit under the per-module partition —
//! `WOLF_MIDEND=0`, the mode lobo builds in while #146 is open), while
//! the native tier ran the same program by importing the symbol
//! (#116). The LLVM emitter now takes an out-of-subset referee's
//! address through the same mangled-symbol declaration a cross-object
//! CALL uses; a driver test pins the per-module partition itself,
//! this file pins the shape on every lane. The two rounds are D68's
//! contract consumed exactly as lobo's budget helper consumes it: a
//! roomy cap joins `normal`, a 64-unit cap joins `fault(alloc-
//! contract)` — read through `is_alloc_contract()` in the leaf, mapped
//! to a small integer for the entry.

use work

fn main() -> !int {
    let a = work.run(100, 1000000)
    let b = work.run(100, 64)
    print("normal={a} breach={b}")
    if a == 0 && b == 2 { 0 } else { 1 }
}
